course: dictionary
lesson: 5633
title: One word, many Lincolns
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Lincoln is a proper noun. It is the name of a particular person or place, so it always starts with a capital letter. One spelling can name different things, so the context tells you which Lincoln is meant.
explain: Look at the clues around it. «Abraham Lincoln, a US president, died in 1865» tells you it is a person. «Lincoln Cathedral in England» tells you it is a place, a city in England.
explain: Ask yourself: who or what is this sentence about? Then look for clues like «president», «cathedral» or a first name. Those clues tell you which Lincoln you are reading about.
fact: Lincoln is a proper noun, so it always starts with a capital letter.
fact: Abraham Lincoln was the 16th President of the United States, and he led the country during the American Civil War.
fact: Lincoln is also a city in the east of England, famous for its cathedral and castle.
fact: Lincoln is the capital of Nebraska in the USA, and it is also a surname and a first name.
fact: «Lincoln Memorial» is a famous monument in Washington, D.C.
exercise: «Abraham Lincoln, a US president, died in 1865, long before computers existed.» Who is Lincoln in this sentence? | A city in Nebraska | A first name for a girl | A castle in England | *A US president, Abraham Lincoln
exercise: «Lincoln Cathedral in England was probably the tallest building in the world for about 200 years.» What kind of Lincoln is this? | A person's first name | *A city in England | A US president | A monument in Washington
exercise: Mia says Lincoln must always be a person. Is she right? | *No, Lincoln can also be a city in England or in Nebraska | Yes, because it has a capital letter | Yes, Lincoln is always a US president
test: Why does Lincoln always start with a capital letter? | Because it is always the first word of a sentence | Because all nouns start with capitals | Because it is a very long word | *Because it is a proper noun, the name of a particular person or place
test: «The Lincoln Memorial» is a famous monument in which city? | Lincoln, England | Lincoln, the first name | *Washington, D.C. | Lincoln, Nebraska
exam: «News of Lincoln's death in 1865 took about 12 days to reach Europe.» Which Lincoln is meant here? | A first name for a boy | The city of Lincoln in England | *Abraham Lincoln, the 16th US President | The Lincoln Cathedral spire
